@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Payflow — Send USDC on Ethereum
+
+A single-purpose dApp: connect a wallet, pay an address or ENS name in USDC, and
+see your USDC and ETH balances while you do it. Self-custodial — the transfer is
+a plain `transfer()` from the user's wallet to the recipient. No contracts of our
+own, no approvals, no intermediary.
+
+The product is `/pay`; `/` redirects there.
+
+## Stack
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript |
+| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 with semantic color tokens (light/dark from the OS) |
+| Chain access | wagmi 2 + viem 2 |
+| Wallets | RainbowKit 2 |
+| Data/caching | TanStack Query (via wagmi) |
+
+## Chain and token
+
+Ethereum **mainnet** only.
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| USDC | `0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48` — 6 decimals |
+| ETH/USD price | Chainlink `0x5f4eC3Df9cbd43714FE2740f5E3616155c5b8419` |
+| USDC/USD price | Chainlink `0x8fFfFfd4AfB6115b954Bd326cbe7B4BA576818f6` |
+
+All amounts are held as base units (`bigint`) and only converted at the edges
+with `parseUnits`/`formatUnits`. Nothing renders base units.
+
+USD values come from Chainlink read directly onchain, so pricing needs no API key
+and shares the app's RPC. A feed that hasn't updated within twice its published
+heartbeat is labelled stale in the UI rather than shown as current; a feed that
+can't be read at all is labelled unavailable rather than silently dropped.
+
+## Setup
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # fill in the RPC url
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000/pay
+```
+
+### Environment
+
+| Variable | Required | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` | for production | Dedicated mainnet RPC. Without it viem falls back to a public gateway that rate limits under real traffic. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | recommended | From [Reown Cloud](https://cloud.reown.com). Without it the app offers only injected, Coinbase and Safe wallets — every other option connects over WalletConnect, and listing them without a project id would render dead buttons. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | for production | Canonical origin, used for `metadataBase` and OG/Twitter card URLs. |
+
+```bash
+npm run build   # production build (also typechecks)
+npm run lint
+npm start
+```
+
+## How the payment flow behaves
+
+**Recipient.** Accepts a hex address or an ENS name. Names resolve onchain on
+mainnet and the resolved address is displayed before you can submit — that
+address is what gets submitted, not the string. A pasted address is
+reverse-resolved to its ENS name when it has one. Every rejection states its
+reason: bad length, failed checksum, a name with no address record, an ENS
+lookup that couldn't complete. Sends to the zero address and to the USDC
+contract itself are blocked; sends to your own address warn but are allowed.
+
+**Amount.** Parsed in USDC's 6 decimals, with more-than-6-decimals, non-numeric,
+zero, and over-balance each getting their own message. A `Max` button fills the
+exact balance. The USD value of what you typed sits under the field.
+
+**Gas.** The form estimates the transfer's gas against the live fee market and
+shows the cost in ETH and USD before you sign — which is why the ETH balance is
+on screen. An account with no ETH is told so instead of being sent to a wallet
+that will reject it.
+
+**One primary action at a time.** The button is *Connect wallet* → *Switch to
+Ethereum* → *Send USDC*, never two at once. When it's disabled it says why
+directly underneath, so it is never a dead button with no explanation.
+
+**One pending state.** The button stays busy from click through wallet
+signature, receipt, *and* the balance refetch — `isPending` clearing when the
+wallet hands back a hash doesn't end it. It's released in `finally`, so a
+rejected signature can't wedge the form. A mined-but-reverted transaction is
+reported as such.
+
+**Errors.** Wallet rejections, insufficient gas, RPC rate limits and ERC-20
+reverts (including USDC's blacklist and pause paths) are translated to plain
+sentences and shown next to the action that failed.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/
+  app/                 routes, metadata, icon + OG image generation
+  components/          UI — PayView composes BalancePanel + PayForm
+  hooks/               useBalances, usePrices, useRecipient, useNow
+  lib/                 config (chain/token/feeds), wagmi, format, amount, errors
+```
+
+`src/lib/config.ts` is the single place the chain, the token and the price feeds
+are defined.
+
+## Notes
+
+- `serverExternalPackages` in `next.config.ts` covers `@coinbase/cdp-sdk` and
+  `@base-org/account`, which arrive transitively through RainbowKit's Base
+  Account connector and reference optional `@x402/*` peers this app never loads.
+- The wagmi config imports RainbowKit's client-only connector helpers, so it
+  can't be imported from a server component. The root layout forwards the raw
+  cookie header to `Providers`, which restores the connection state inside the
+  client graph for both the SSR pass and hydration.
+- Not affiliated with Circle.
